  "summary": "Four supplied candidates directly apply contrastive learning (representation learning with paired positive and negative examples) to estimating agricultural yield. [V0048] is a deployment study on ToxiBench reporting F1=0.83 (Brennan et al., 2018); [V0047] evaluates on CellLife with AUROC 0.76 (Adebayo et al., 2026); [V0046] evaluates on LedgerGuard with test MAE 0.69 (Haddad et al., 2025); [V0045] evaluates on AgriSat-4 with accuracy 0.62 (Gupta et al., 2024). Reported metrics are not directly comparable across studies (F1, AUROC, MAE, accuracy) and datasets differ (ToxiBench, CellLife, LedgerGuard, AgriSat-4). Only four candidates match both the requested method and topic; the fifth-ranked candidate [V0040] targets the same topic but uses boosted decision-tree ensembles (ToxiBench, MAE 0.61) and is included as a non-contrastive comparator. Other candidates either apply the contrastive method to unrelated topics (e.g., [V0094], [V0142], [V0239], [V0214]) or address agricultural yield with different methods (e.g., [V0032], [V0034], [V0036], [V0043]), or mention contrastive yield work only as prior work (e.g., [V0015], [V0217], [V0066]) and are therefore excluded from the direct-evidence ranking.",
